  "description": "\nSummary of Proposed Works\n\nThe proposed works comprise minor internal alterations to a flat within Ben Jonson House, including the installation of new full-height internal doors (one sliding pocket door to the bathroom and two hinged doors to the bedroom and upper penthouse room), the removal of an existing non-structural kitchen peninsular wall and associated suspended bulkhead, and the removal of a small non-structural nib wall within the bedroom.\n\nA new bespoke kitchen will be installed within the existing footprint, including a reinstated peninsular formed with an overhanging worktop to create a breakfast bar with seating facing the dining area.\n\nThe bedroom layout will be reconfigured to provide an enlarged built-in wardrobe with an integrated utility cupboard.\n\nAll works are internal, non-structural, and will be carried out in a manner that respects the character and detailing of the original Barbican interiors.",
